neighborhood (\\(N_1\\)) and the swap neighborhood (\\(N_2\\)) (both used in the first phase) as well as the constrained-three-cyclic-exchange neighborhood (\\(N_3\\)).\n\n**Constrained-three-cyclic-exchange neighborhood (\\(N_3\\)) [40]:** This neighborhood is induced by the three-cyclic-exchange operator \\(cyclic(v,u,w)\\) that displaces three vertices \\(u \\in V_j\\), \\(v \\in V_i\\) and \\(w \\in V_h\\) to another color classes \\(V_j\\), \\(V_h\\) and \\(V_i\\) in a cyclic way. With no restriction, the three-cyclic-exchange operator leads to a very large neighborhood (whose size is bounded by \\(O(|V|^3)\\)). In order to reduce the computational burden of this operator, we impose the following constraints: 1) vertex \\(v\\) is a conflicting vertex; 2) before and after moving the vertex \\(v\\), the difference of the conflicting edges induced by the vertex \\(v\\) is no more than 2; for the movement of the vertex \\(u\\) and \\(w\\), the sum of the changes of the conflicting edges induced by \\(u\\) and \\(w\\) is at most 2. The constrained-three-cyclic-exchange neighborhood \\(N_3\\) is given as follows.\n\n<visual_element id=\"e1\">\n\n**Equation (10): Constrained-three-cyclic-exchange neighborhood**\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nN_3(s)=\\{s\\oplus cyclic(v,u,w):\\;&v\\in V_i,\\ u\\in V_j,\\ w\\in V_h,\\ i\\ne j,\\ i\\ne h,\\ j\\ne h,\\\\\n&v\\in C(s)\\ne\\varnothing,\\\\\n&A[v][j]-A[v][i]\\leq 2,\\\\\n&A[u][h]-A[u][j]+A[w][i]-A[w][h]\\leq 2\\}\n\\end{aligned}\n\\tag{10}\n\\]\n\n</visual_element>\n\nwhere \\(A\\) is a matrix of size \\(n\\times k\\) where each element \\(A[v][i]\\) records the number of vertices adjacent to \\(v\\) in color class \\(V_i\\) (\\(1\\leq i\\leq k\\)).\n\n14--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTDK Konferencia (https://csikvarip.web.elte.hu/tdk_2024_palyazatok.pdf)\nciteturn4search17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.0 years ago; | Pályázó Jörg Áron | Cím Becslés egy új csomócsalád pálcaszámá